# --- MATLAB ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.asv
*.mex*
slprj/

# --- OS junk --------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db

# --- PDFs -----------------------------------------------------------------
# No PDF belongs in the code repository. This covers three separate cases:
#   1. Third-party publisher PDFs (e.g. s00161-022-01167-8.pdf, the Djordjic
#      et al. 2023 paper) -- redistributing them would infringe copyright.
#   2. Manuscript builds (e.g. cas-sc-template.pdf) -- the manuscripts live in
#      their own repositories.
#   3. Figures written by the benchmark and plotting scripts. These are build
#      products: rerun the producing script (see the script-to-artifact map in
#      the README) to regenerate any of them.
*.pdf

# --- Precomputed collision tensors ----------------------------------------
# The serialized operators in src/precalc/ are build products, not source.
# They run to tens of MB (polyatomic DSMC) or tens of GB (monatomic
# hard-sphere sweeps) and are regenerated on demand -- see the README section
# "Regenerating the precomputed tensors".
src/precalc/

# --- LaTeX / build logs ---------------------------------------------------
texput.log
*.aux
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz

# --- Scratch outputs written by the benchmark and plotting scripts --------
fig_transport_fits_marker_check.png
perf_contraction_timings.csv

# Generated result artifacts (regenerated by the benchmark scripts). The one
# exception is the transport-fits sampling data, which is shipped: it is the
# input of plot_transport_fits_paper.m, not only its output, and regenerating
# it from scratch needs the cached operators. Note the rule is results/* and
# not results/ -- git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded.
results/*
!results/fig_transport_fits_data.mat
